A||N||3||rigdonhome||Another V8 Tranny Question||||6||
Z||000000||rigdonhome||08-20-2001||08:30 PM||||I'm the new guy that keeps asking, Why? Why? Why? like a little kid...  (Secretly I just like wasting bandwidth!)<P>There seem to be some issues with the V8 swap and the Fiero trannies...  The N* guys say that the best way to go (for a number of reasons) is with the stock N* complete motor/trans combination.  This would be great but while I'm breaking all the rules I have to stay with a manual, just for fun's sake!!!  I'm not knocking autos, I have just always had them in all my project vehicles, and I want something new!<P>Is there a heavier-duty 5-speed available that can be used with the Fiero V8 swap?  Even if it's more difficult and costly, it would probably be worth it in my case.  Some will disagree and argue that the Getrag? 5-speed will hold up, but there are 2 reasons that I think this won't hold true in my case:<P>1)  I plan to eventually make 450 horse with a supercharged LT1, and that's probably the high limit of what I've read the stock 5-speed will hold up to.  (Please correct me if I'm wrong!)<P>2)  I drive it like I MEAN it!!!  I know everyone thinks they drive their cars hard, but for me my drive to work or the grocery is the highlight of my day!  My engine sees the red line at LEAST 5 times every single time I drive it, the clutch gets dumpet at LEAST 3 times, and I lay at LEAST 2 sets of black marks each and every time I get in a vehicle.  For no explainable reason.  It's just in my blood.  Let me quote the guy that's built all of my high-performance transmissions:  "Well, normally I would say the T5 would hold up in a V8 S10, but with YOU behind the wheel, we need to beef that up quite a bit."<P>Are there beef-up parts for the 5-speed that make it hold up better?<P>Any suggestions???<P>Cheers,<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black<BR>5 speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Cherry!||||reg||6
Z||000001||DRH||08-21-2001||12:24 AM||||My understanding is there are some <B>slightly</B> stronger versions of the Getrag in other cars. I don't think it's anything that would give you more than a couple of extra grocery runs with the combo of one and two above. You probably need to start a tranny collection like rockcrawl has in about the 10th post in this thread: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012963.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012963.html</A>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Clutches and CV joints could cause problems in your scenario too...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jimmy||08-21-2001||03:20 AM||||Ask anyone who knows me or rides with me, I drive my V8 5speed like I mean it.  One thing you don't have to worry about is dropping the clutch, there really is no point caquse at 1500 RPM you can definitely spin the tires all day long without dropping the clutch.  BTW I have 275-300hp and 345 ftlbs of torque.  I have over 2500 miles on this setup with quite a bit of hard driving and so far no problem, lets just see how many years I can get out of it.<P>BTW, if you are going to have 450hp look for something other than centerforce df, luk, ram clutches all of these slip at some point.  Mine is a centerforce DF and it will slip every once in a while, not a real bad slip, just one I can barely notice or get a wiff of.<P>Jim<BR>87 GT<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8||||reg||1
Z||000003||JayUSA77||08-21-2001||02:28 PM||||rigdonhome your in the same hole i am. im putting a LS1 with nitrous and having about 550 to 600 HP but no transaxle can hold up to that massive abuse that i have found. Send my a email at jayusa77@home.com and well keep in touch and see if we cant help eachother out.<BR>j<BR><P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
